      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Cost &amp; Timing Insights: Moving Household Goods by Train versus Road to Bokaro</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p><strong>Bokaro Relocations: Train vs Road Transport</strong></p>

<h3>Pricing</h3>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Road freight usually charges a flat rate based on distance and volume.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>In Bokaro, a standard household move might cost ₹4,000–₹8,000 for a 10‑day haul.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Train freight, however, is calculated per kilogram, often around ₹5–₹7 per kg.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>For a 1,000‑kg load, the <strong>bike parcel in train price</strong> would be roughly ₹5,000, slightly cheaper than a long‑haul road trip, especially when factoring in fuel surcharges.</span></li></ul>

<h3>Transit Time</h3>
<p>Road transport is flexible and can start immediately, completing the move within 2–3 days for intra‑state trips. Train schedules, however, depend on rail timetables; a typical Bokaro‑to‑Delhi move takes 3–4 days, plus waiting time for loading and unloading. If time is critical, road is the faster choice.</p>

<h3>Safety and Security
</h3><p>Road movers often use sealed containers and GPS tracking, but theft or damage during traffic congestion remains a risk. Train transport keeps goods in dedicated freight cars with minimal handling, reducing breakage. Both modes require <strong>IBA approved packers and movers</strong> to ensure proper packing and insurance coverage.</p>

<h3>Paperwork and Compliance</h3>
<p>Road freight requires a simple Bill of Lading and a commercial invoice. Train freight demands additional rail freight documents, including a Railway Cargo Receipt and customs clearance for interstate moves. While paperwork for trains is more extensive, it provides an audit trail that can be useful for insurance claims.</p>

<h3>Environmental Impact</h3>
<p>Trains are more energy‑efficient, emitting fewer CO₂ per ton‑kilometer. For eco‑conscious families, choosing rail can reduce the carbon footprint of a Bokaro relocation.</p>

<h3>When to Choose Which?</h3>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
